; THE ASH YARD - a campaign's own room, and the second map the project has (CONTENT_PIPELINE.md P2).
;
; DELIBERATELY A DIFFERENT SHAPE from maps/cellar.map: wider than it is deep, one long wall with a
; door in it rather than a hall split down the middle, and the rubble in a drift along the south
; edge instead of in patches. If the board can play this one without a scene edit, the room really
; is data.
;
; The wall stops short of the south end, so the yard is ONE room with a long way round in it. That
; is deliberate too: a shut door blocks exactly like a wall (Edge.Door), and a yard whose only way
; across is a shut one is two sealed rooms and a fight nobody can reach. The gap is the route and
; the door is the shortcut somebody forces (B4) - which is the same thing the cellar's east
; chambers do, and the reason that map has a gap at ITS far end.
;
; SAME FORMAT, DOUBLE RESOLUTION (EDGE_WALLS.md) - squares on the odd/odd positions and the lines
; between them on the rest. What is new is the NUMBERS: 1-9 are spawn slots, and an encounter says
; who stands on each (P4). The map says where; it never says who, so the same yard can be four
; hounds one chapter and a ghoul the next.
;
;   .  floor      ~  difficult ground   #  rock      @  the hero starts
;   1-9 a spawn   |  wall up a line     -  wall along a line   x  door, shut   +  a corner

